��i<?php exit; ?>a:2:{s:7:"content";O:8:"stdClass":24:{s:2:"ID";i:5363;s:11:"post_author";s:1:"1";s:9:"post_date";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:03";s:13:"post_date_gmt";s:19:"2026-04-01 09:57:03";s:12:"post_content";s:1358:"<ul class="blog-details__list"><li>Record pairing etiquette in writing</li><li>Measure WIP, not seat time</li><li>Offer stipends for home ergonomics</li></ul><ol class="blog-details__list"><li>Record pairing etiquette in writing</li><li>Measure WIP, not seat time</li><li>Offer stipends for home ergonomics</li></ol><h2 class="blog-details__h2">Next steps for leaders</h2><h2 class="blog-details__h2">Patterns that hold up in delivery</h2><p>Tooling—shared IDEs, async review habits, and crisp story splits—matters more than mandating two days in beige cubicles.</p><blockquote class="blog-details__blockquote"><p>Security left-shifted is cheaper than security as a gate: lightweight checklists beat forty-page PDFs nobody reads.</p></blockquote><blockquote class="blog-details__blockquote"><p>Building for regulated environments means every design choice is tested against security, auditability, and long-term maintainability—not just feature velocity.</p></blockquote><p>If you are planning a similar initiative, start with a thin end-to-end slice, instrument it in production, and expand scope only when telemetry supports the next bet.</p><p>Hybrid offices tempt managers to favor whoever is physically present. Pair programming policies need explicit fairness so remote engineers are not permanent drivers.</p><hr class="blog-details__divider" />";s:10:"post_title";s:34:"Pair Programming in Hybrid Offices";s:12:"post_excerpt";s:308:"Pair Programming in Hybrid Offices — Hybrid offices tempt managers to favor whoever is physically present. Pair programming policies need explicit fairness so remote engineers are not permanent drivers. Tooling—shared IDEs, async review habits, and crisp story splits—matters more than mandating two…";s:11:"post_status";s:7:"publish";s:14:"